<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sīmus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιμός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>flat-nosed</i>, <i>snub-nosed</i> (cf. silus). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">avibus, serpentibus, piscibus, foramina tantum
					ad olfactus sine naribus, et hinc cognomina Simorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 59, § 158</span></i>
			: pecus Nerei, i. e. <i>dolphins</i>, Liv.
			Andron. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 335, 22</span></i> (Trag. Rel.
			p. 1 Rib.); cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rostrum delphini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 8, 7, § 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capellae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 10, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer simā nare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					6, 39, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cels. 8, 10,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i><span class="en">Verg. M.
			107</span></i>.</div>
